  "displayName": "sgm-005 default band (equipment-scoped catch-all)",
  "description": "FIX 5 (2026-07-31) — sgm-005 (Krauss-Maffei CX 130, v4-SGM-010) had NO recipe of its own, so its hot-runner was judged against a band authored for a different machine and its actual process sat exactly ON an alarm line (measured hotrunnerTempC mean 240.03 degC = the action-upper it was being judged against). A real machine does not hold its setpoint on its own alarm threshold. This recipe re-centres the bands on THIS machine's real setpoint: nozzle SOLL 240 degC (machines-sgm/src/config.ts:373 nozzleSetpointC=240, barrel [210,218,228,235]) so 240 sits in the MIDDLE of its band, not on the edge. Widths mirror the sgm-004 default. mouldTempC band [80,90] is the PA-resin norm (mould TCU target 87.5 degC, MOULD_TCU_TARGET_C). Only the two signals we can calibrate from the machine spec are bound here; pressures/cushion/partMass stay dormant (no per-machine drawing/process sheet yet) so no un-calibrated band can raise a false alarm.",
  "match": {
    "equipment": "sgm-005"
  },
